§12.11's composability, measured on the seated tower

   stage    cells  composable  fraction   printed  source -> target
  Λ8          976           0    0.0000    0.0000  (n,l,k,2S) -> (e,f,g)  OK
  Λ9         1654        1169    0.7068    0.7068  (n,l,k,2S) -> (e,f,g,2S')  OK
  Λ10        2535        2050    0.8087    0.8087  (n,l,k,2S) -> (e,f,g,2S')  OK
  Λ12       70905       46740    0.6592    0.6592  (n,l,k,2S,2Jc) -> (e,f,g,2S',2K)  OK

  Λ11 and Λ13 are not reproduced by any pairing an exhaustive same-size sweep over the
  plausible coordinate pools tried. Reported, not smoothed.

WHAT THIS DECIDES ABOUT §12.11's TABLE
  The table gives Λ10 as 'no — no source seniority exists' and the prose concludes
  'Λ9 is the only stage of the tower that composes' and 'Λ9 sits alone'.
  MEASURED: Λ10 composes at 0.8087 — 2050 of 2535 cells —
  USING THE SAME SOURCE AND TARGET SHAPES THAT MAKE Λ9 WORK, and that is its PEAK.
  Λ12 composes at 0.6592 on the shapes one axis wider. So the compendium's series and the
  main volume's table are two different predicates wearing one word.

  REGISTER 314's CLAIM IS UNTOUCHED: 'an axis can be exact and not composable; none is
  composable and not exact' does not depend on which stages compose. What falls is the
  supporting evidence — 'Λ10 was never structurally barred' and 'Λ9 is not alone' — and
  that is the correction the retraction audit recorded. The claim survives; the evidence
  does not. Nothing is repaired here.
